From 5de53b78267abc3f10eaac8b749f9e7ff81975f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:48:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(turning): allow threading passes to start in front of the
 end face

Keep revolve::lattice strictly inside the bar domain [d_lo, d_hi] by
removing the post-filter re-insertion of window endpoints w0 and w1, so
free air past the end face is never judged as rest. Compute k_hi in
thread_planned_in from the unclamped f.station_of(p.top_z) so a
threading pass can place lead-in lattice points in free air in front of
the end face while keeping ref_top, valley phase detection, and the
empty-window refusal clamped to the bar.

Fixes #2879
